// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2003785415" "You met the whole gang, and even helped out a newer member.  Now you need to meet up with Twinshot outside where she's hanging out."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3686536389" "Thanks for stopping by.  Everyone seemed to like your style, so they wanted me to ask you if you wanted to join up with our team.  You know, friends and all that stuff.  How's that sound, kiddo?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MsLiberty 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P817304945" "Hi there!  I can help you with all of your training needs.  Come to me anytime you feel your personal training is - I'm sorry, what was that?"
// Answer Text :
"P3087448298" "I'm Twinshot's friend.  She said you could give me pointers?"
// Page LibertyOne Text :
"P227685705" "Oh, you're Twin's friend?  I know I've seen you around before, but I didn't know you were hanging out with her.  Let me tell something about that girl... She's got a good heart, you know?<br><br>Any friend of Twinshot is a friend of mine.  What would you like me to help you with?"
// Answer Text :
"P798428999" "Why do I come to trainers for leveling?"
// Page LibertyTwo Text :
"P3155765060" "A bunch of us here in Paragon City like helping other people.  For instance, did you know there's a place where you can actually talk with other heroes just like you and I?  I think they call it the Help Channel.  But back to what I was saying.<br><br>When you gain a new level of experience, you may not know how to push your powers to that new level.  However, that's what we trainers help you do.  We show you all the things you can do with your powers."
// Answer Text :
"P681398769" "How do I gain levels?"
// Page LibertyThree Text :
"P824944537" "As you perform tasks for the safety of the people of Paragon City, you'll gain more and more experience.  Once you've had your fill of learning the ins-and-outs of crimefighting, you'll increase your security level.  That's when you want to come to me or another trainer and we'll show you how to take your powers up to the next level, too."
// Answer Text :
"P4291417052" "How do I know when to come to you?"
// Page LibertyFour Text :
"P3785865765" "You'll have a mental indicator letting you know it's time.  Think of it like a flashing arrow.  After we talk, you can decide where you want to apply your newfound powers.  Sometimes you'll want to increase a power you already have, and other times you might even learn a new one.  In the end, it's pretty much up to you.  We're only here to help guide you along the way."
// Answer Text :
"P4217534077" "You mentioned others.  Where are they?"
// Page LibertyDone Text :
"P3136306941" "They're all over Paragon City.  You can usually find someone in just about every district.  How about you pay a visit to Blue Steel.  He's over in Kings Row, which is a short tram ride away.<br><br>How about you go pay him a visit and let him know that Ms. Liberty sent you.  Kinda the way Twin did earlier."
// Answer Text :
"P3113720303" "I can do that.  Thanks, Ms. Liberty."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - BlueSteel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1205870089" "Hello there, citizen.  Are you in need of training suggestions today?"
// Answer Text :
"P3774511545" "Actually, Ms. Liberty sent me to you for more pointers."
// Page SteelOne Text :
"P1935970549" "Oh, I see.  I take it you're an up-and-coming hero?  Good!  This city can use all it can get.  As you can tell, this part of the city is still struggling to get the street crime under control, which is why I'm here.  What kind of pointers were you looking for?"
// Answer Text :
"P893384462" "That tram I came in on... Does it only go here?"
// Page SteelTwo Text :
"P591031863" "Nah, the trams go to all different parts of the city.  You should be able to find a monorail station in just about  every district in the city and they'll take you to nearly every other one as well.<br><br>Just make sure you don't get off at the wrong stop.  Some places can be a bit too dangerous for those new to the area.  As a matter of fact, even here in Kings Row we have to deal with street gangs that simply don't respect the law.<br><br>Speaking of... would you be willing to do your civic duty as a hero and help take care of some of these gangs for us?"
// Answer Text :
"P322455795" "Of course! What do you need me to do?"
// Page SteelThree Text :
"P1475708605" "All throughout the streets you'll find a variety of hoodlums.  However, the ones that are the most blatant violators of the law as of late are a gang that calls themselves the Skulls.  They're pretty easy to spot - each of them wears a piece of a human skull on their face.<br><br>You should be able to find them hanging out all around the police station here in Freedom Plaza. On your way back to Atlas Park, could you send a number of them to the hospital? We'll be sure to have a police escort waiting for them once they get patched up."
// Answer Text :
"P1972758011" "Absolutely.  Thanks for the advice, Blue Steel."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P938591635" "Hey there, kiddo.  So I was thinking... You held your own pretty well with those Arachnos guys storming the place last time, right?  But you could always use a couple of pointers here and there.<br><br>Now I could show you a thing or two, but I'm not really a good teacher.  However, I know someone who I could put you in touch with.  Interested?"
// AcceptString :
"P3272127629" "Sure.  Where do I find him?"
// SendOffString :
"P552277171" "You can find HER outside City Hall.  The name's Ms. Liberty.  You may have already met her before, but the gal's pretty busy helping people out so you may not have had a real chance to get to know her.  You let her know that you're a friend of Twinshot and she'll likely take some time out to chat with you."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1412550875" "<color deepskyblue>Ongoing Training</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P218680802" "Talk to Ms. Liberty"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2024599071" "If you tell Ms. Liberty that you're a friend of mine, I'm pretty sure she'll take a couple of minutes out of her day to give you some pointers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4178434779" "You've been given some pointers from Ms. Liberty on how to train yourself to become more powerful.  Now she wants you to go talk to Blue Steel."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1600808129" "Ride the Monorail from Atlas Park to Kings Row."
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3480930229" "So, Libby wants you to talk with Blue Steel now?  I should have thought of that.<br><br>Okay, in order to get there you'll want to go to the tram station in Atlas Park and take it to Kings Row. Steel isn't too far away from there."
// VolumeDescription :
"P1201268524" "Use your map to find the Monorail Station"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P309058268" "You've arrived at the Atlas Park monorail station.  Now use the tram to travel to Kings Row and talk with Blue Steel at the police station."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3749074087" "Talk to Blue Steel"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1994712465" "Once you're in Kings Row, you should be able to pull up a map and find where Blue Steel is.  You'll spot him by the helmet."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2314899806" "You talked with Blue Steel and were told about the trams that are all over the city.  Before you were done, though, he asked if you could help deal with the Skulls that are causing problems for the city."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3222019380" "Defeat Skulls in Kings Row!"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2376962324" "So you're saying Steel wanted you to help him with the Skulls?  You might want to watch out... Those ones over in Kings Row are a bit more tough than here in Atlas Park.  Then again, I'll leave that up to you to decide, you know?"
// VillainDescription :
"P2766093955" "Defeat {Remain} Skulls"
// VillainSingularDescription :
"P1385723178" "One last Skull remains"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1519383460" "You managed to get a few more Skulls off the streets and made the city that much safer."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2592337641" "You're back, kiddo.  I'm hoping Liberty and Steel managed to drive a few of those pointers home in that thick noggin of yours.<br><br>Hahaha... I'm joshing with you.  Remember, though.  Whenever you feel you need to up your powers a bit more, always hit a trainer.  Even if you have to ride from one end of the city to the other, it's worth it.  Get in touch with me in a while, kid.  I might have something else in store for you."
// RandomFameString :
"P4264314277" "Hey, didn't I just see {HeroName} on the tram?  It's kinda nice knowing people like that are keeping the trains safe."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SecurityTerminal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2362759500" "<color orange>This console is linked to the security system that Proton recently put in place due to the Arachnos intruders gaining entry so easily the last time you were here.  It would seem that it was installed a little too late.</color><br><br><color red>WARNING: INTRUDER ALERT!  INTRUDER ALERT!  CONTACT ALL SHINING STARS.</color><br><br><color orange>There are several live camera feeds currently being displayed on the console's screen.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1099992643" "Scan the first floor"
// Page FirstFloor Text :
"P3533990043" "<color orange>You observe the cameras on the first floor of the facility.<br><br> The entrance to the facility seems relatively undamaged.  The camera shows you standing at the console looking at the screen.  Before the elevators to the next floor you see a group of Arachnos thugs apparently waiting in ambush.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3986848914" "Scan the second floor"
// Page SecondFloor Text :
"P1111254287" "<color orange>You observe the cameras on the second floor of the facility.<br><br> Dillo appears to be fending off multiple Arachnos attacks.  Although he appears to be holding his own, his movements would appear as if he may have suffered injuries and will need some help.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3568532887" "Scan the third floor"
// Page ThirdFloor Text :
"P607872671" "<color orange>You observe the cameras on the third floor of the facility.<br><br>The top floor is swarming with Arachnos!  In the far end, both Proton and Flambeaux seem to be holed up near another console.  Proton is tapping furiously on the keyboard whilst Flambeaux is holding at bay the more brave of the soldiers.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4291677466" "Lock down the terminal"
// Page LockDown Text :
"P1127840748" "<color orange>As you lock down the terminal to prevent the Arachnos agents from gaining access to it, you see a shadow pass by the camera display on the first floor cameras.<br><br>Looking more closely, you see that the movement is right next to you!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1785163170" "Look around for the shadow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - TwinshotPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3942312810" "Okay, looks like the outside is clear.  If there was any backup outside, they're probably all taking a coffee break.  That's not usually the way Arachnos works, but let's not look a gift horse in the mouth.<br><br>What did you find on the cameras?"
// Answer Text :
"P1805431062" "Dillo is facing off against a bunch of them upstairs."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2817287805" "Well why didn't you say so? Let's get going and help that little guy, pronto!"
// Answer Text :
"P4126636940" "Let's go!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DilloPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2700119916" "*hoorb*<br><br>You are friends with I who am Dillo!  Too many holes were - as you Earthlings say - filled with jelly!<br><br>But the one who is Dillo can seal the leaks."
// Answer Text :
"P4275587401" "Did you say you... healed yourself?"
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P274679652" "I am giving negativity.  I am with the healing, as you Earthlings say, but I am still pushing air through holes.<br><br>I need to adjust pressurization or I will fall down like a ripe banana!<br><br>*hoorgb* No, no... that is not what you Earthlings say.  I must say that we need to use a respressurizer or I will be a banana split!  YES!  HAHA!  That is it!"
// Answer Text :
"P4194165961" "Pressurizer!  Got it.  Let's find one!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ProtonPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2619955005" "Quickly!  I need you to access my computer while I dictate these calculations!"
// Answer Text :
"P3453223164" "What?  What am I supposed to do?"
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P2990449262" "Just use my computer terminal!  I am aligning my armor system to fire off an EMP burst that should affect the Arachnos communications networks they employ.  This should send a pulse into their ears loud enough to render them in a state of shock.<br><br>Hurry, {HeroName}!  We don't have much time!"
// Answer Text :
"P434760014" "I'm on it!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SecurityTerminalTwo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P303356293" "<color orange>The terminal has only one line blinking on the screen.</color><br><br>Enter Pulse Charge Frequency Code."
// Answer Text :
"P1598300160" "Proton!  What's the code?"
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P290552598" "<color orange>Proton yells out the code and you quickly type it in.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2142244500" "Alpha - One - Prime"
// Page ConversationNode2 Text :
"P3336674752" "<color orange>The screen flashes for a moment followed by the words:</color><br><br>Pulse Frequency Incoming."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P201413204" "How's it going, kiddo.  I was thinking we could patrol the city, you know, doing our civic duty and all that hero-ey goodness.  But seriously though, doing our part to help stamp out crime will go a long way towards helping the city's future.  And I for one like the idea of having a bright and shiny new future, you know? Also, while we're patrolling, I'd like to ask your feelings about that Grym character.  Him showing up when he did was a bit coincidental, don't you think?  I mean it's one thing to --<br><br><color orange>Twinshot touches the earpiece she's wearing and pauses for a moment.</color><br><br>Heads up, kiddo.  Proton is sending out a distress call.  Says he needs our help ASAP."
// AcceptString :
"P2866163473" "Distress call?  What can we do to help him?"
// SendOffString :
"P1827496179" "<color orange>Twinshot gestures to you that she's listening  to the message.<br><br></color>Oh that's not good...<br><br><color orange>Twinshot hands move to her pistols faster than your eye can follow, finishing with a flourishing twirl.<br><br></color>Bad news, kiddo.  Looks like Arachnos decided to come back for Round Two.  From his message, it sound like it's not just a scouting team, either.  What in the heck are they doing all the way over here... and why?<br><br>We can figure that out later.  For now we're passing on the patroling.  Instead, you're going in through the front while I'm taking out any perimeter defenses they've set up.  I'll meet you inside."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4033522371" "Help Defend the Shining Stars' Base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1162346171" "Hey there, kiddo.  I sure hope you're calling to let me know that you're okay and you've personally taken care of all those spider goons.  If not, we'll have to jabber-jaw later seeing that our home is under attack, you know?"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1593343679" "<color deepskyblue>A Spider Infestation</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1305880811" "From the minor blast marks, it would seem Arachnos  used expertly localized explosives to blow open the door.  Now is when you think it might have been a better idea for Twinshot to have joined you."

